"""HX PZ1.27-2x3P ZZ - 2x03 pin header, 1.27 mm pitch, straight, gold-flashed brass square pins.
Bare part, footprinted as a straddle (edge) mount: a small upright board stands between its two
rows, its bottom edge on the insulator, and the long pins go down into the board below.

Datasheet: Shenzhen Hanxia Electronic, specification for approval and drawing HX PZ1.27-2x3P ZZ
(drawing rev A, 2023-07-18; the URL in pcb.toml); JLCPCB/LCSC C22438118 (extended).
Drawing: 0.40 mm square pins (SQ 0.40) at 1.27 +-0.1 mm along the rows, the rows 1.27 mm apart
(end view); the pins run 3.90 +-0.2 mm from the insulator's one face and 2.30 +-0.2 mm from the
other; the insulator is 1.00 mm high, 3.40 mm across the rows (top view) and DIM B = 3.81 +-0.3 mm
long for 3 positions (DIM A, the outer pins' span, 2.54 +-0.2 mm). Recommended PCB layout:
0.65 mm holes at 1.27 x 1.27 mm (+-0.05 mm). Unlisted tolerances: X.XX +-0.20 (title block).
Specifications (same sheet): 1.0 A, AC 500 V withstanding, 1000 MOhm min insulation, 20 mOhm max
contact resistance, -40 to +105 C, PA6T insulator (polyester UL94V-0), brass contacts with gold
flash; maximum processing temperature 240 C for 30-60 s (260 C for 5 s). The LCSC listing gives
the same numbers (insulation height 1 mm, end pin 2.3 mm, mating pin 3.9 mm).

Footprint HX-PZ1.27-2x3P-ZZ_Straddle: the upright board's side. The board stands between the
rows, whose 0.40 mm pins leave 1.27 - 0.40 = 0.87 mm between them, for a 0.8 mm board
(0.79 mm nominal; JLCPCB's +-0.1 mm below 1.0 mm gives 0.7-0.9 mm: from 0.085 mm a side, filled by
the solder, to a 0.03 mm press fit the brass pins take). Its bottom edge rests on the insulator, the
2.30 mm pins lie on SMD pads, odd pins on the front face (F.Cu), even pins on the back (B.Cu), and
the 3.90 mm pins point down into the board below. Pads 0.70 x 2.60 mm (the pin plus 0.15 mm of
side fillet a side, 0.57 mm between pads), from 0.2 mm above the edge (copper to edge) to 2.8 mm,
0.3 mm past the longest pin (2.30 + 0.2 mm). Origin on the board's bottom edge, between the rows;
pin 1 at x = -1.27 mm on the front (a silk bar above its pad), pin 2 behind it. The insulator and the pins on F.Fab/B.Fab;
F.CrtYd/B.CrtYd the pads and the insulator, plus 0.15/0.25 mm. The 3D model (model.py, from the
drawing, embedded) places a 0.79 mm board between the rows.
The other board's 2x03 holes are that board's own footprint (components/micras/WallJoint).

Pins: Pin_1 to Pin_6, 1-3-5 along the front row, 2-4-6 behind them.
"""

P1 = io(Net)
P2 = io(Net)
P3 = io(Net)
P4 = io(Net)
P5 = io(Net)
P6 = io(Net)

Component(
    name="J",
    prefix="J",
    symbol=Symbol(library="HX-PZ1.27-2x3P-ZZ.kicad_sym"),
    footprint=File("HX-PZ1.27-2x3P-ZZ_Straddle.kicad_mod"),
    part=Part(mpn="HX PZ1.27-2x3P ZZ", manufacturer="Hanxia"),
    pins={"Pin_1": P1, "Pin_2": P2, "Pin_3": P3, "Pin_4": P4, "Pin_5": P5, "Pin_6": P6},
)
